# The tokenizer assets are ASCII text (base64 token, space, integer rank per
# line), so git would normally treat them as text and translate line endings on
# checkout. On Windows — the platform this project targets — that would rewrite
# LF to CRLF and corrupt the ranks tiktoken parses out of them. Pin both asset
# types to binary so they round-trip byte-for-byte on every platform.
*.tiktoken -text
*.npz -text
